WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
Speaker 1: Well, ladies and gentlemen, California&nbsp;
Senator Dianne Feinstein at 89 years old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:12.540
will not seek reelection in 2024. This&nbsp;
clears the path for a hotly contested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:18.060
Democratic primary in that state involving&nbsp;
Adam Schiff, Katie Porter and Barbara Lee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.500
as well as others who have already declared&nbsp;
that they are indeed running. We have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:30.360
wondering for some time, is Dianne Feinstein going&nbsp;
to retire now? There are sort of two stories here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:38.160
First, there is the story, as CNBC writes about&nbsp;
Feinstein being the oldest sitting U.S. senator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:44.700
and the longest serving senator. And a growing&nbsp;
appetite among Democrats in various parts of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.380
the country for the next generation of leaders.&nbsp;
Now, what's interesting is the next generation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:55.560
after Dianne Feinstein is still people. You are&nbsp;
in their sixties. So like two generations later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.880
maybe, you know, you understand what I'm&nbsp;
saying? So there's the general desire there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:07.020
The second part, and we want to be respectful when&nbsp;
we talk about this is specifically about Dianne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:13.980
Feinstein and her cognitive state. As for years&nbsp;
now, there have been growing concerns about what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:20.820
is happening with Dianne Feinstein as she is close&nbsp;
to 90 years old. Pretty widespread reports of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:25.860
very quickly, forgetting that she has met people&nbsp;
when she's going through her normal course of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:32.040
being a senator. We have seen a sort of confused&nbsp;
Dianne Feinstein during Senate hearings during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.000
which she will read a question off of a piece of&nbsp;
paper that she doesn't fully seem to understand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.740
and then she will immediately read the same&nbsp;
question again, not realizing that she already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:47.640
asked that one. So it's not something we laugh at.&nbsp;
It's it's a sad situation more than anything. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:54.240
it has also raised concerns among some Democrats&nbsp;
that because of the power of incumbency, that if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.500
she did choose to run again, it could get very&nbsp;
messy and complicated. But none of that is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:03.480
to happen because 89 year old Dianne Feinstein&nbsp;
says this is going to be it for her. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:07.980
when you look at the names of folks that are&nbsp;
currently running here, there are a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:15.240
different names. Some we recognize, for example,&nbsp;
Katie Porter, Adam Schiff, Barbara Lee. Actually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:21.420
Barbara Lee is not on this list. I thought.&nbsp;
Hold on a second. Barbara Lee Senate race.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:29.460
Lee is planning to launch, but has not yet&nbsp;
announced. Okay. There is also a guy named&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:34.380
Barack Obama, Mandela who's running. This is&nbsp;
not in the Democratic side. Remember that in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.120
California it is I believe they call it a jungle&nbsp;
primary where everybody is on the same ballot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:45.240
and the top two vote getters make it to the final&nbsp;
election in November of 2024. So this is a large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.980
list of folks here because of the political&nbsp;
dynamics in California, a very blue state.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:56.640
The Senate election, in practical terms, is the&nbsp;
primary. And it becomes clear from the primary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.380
who is ultimately going to be the senator. And&nbsp;
Katie Porter versus Adam Schiff is going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:06.360
very interesting if, indeed Barbara Lee announces&nbsp;
that she is running and she's expected to in a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:12.900
days. This is going to be a primary with numerous&nbsp;
Democratic heavy hitters. And I am not taking a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:17.580
position on it at this time. I genuinely don't&nbsp;
know what to expect from such a primary. Adam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:23.340
Schiff, Barbara Lee and Katie Porter, all three&nbsp;
relatively well known Schiff, probably the best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.860
known. Although Katie Porter social media presence&nbsp;
is significant. Lot of viral moments. She's very,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:34.080
very good in hearings. So that's going to be an&nbsp;
interesting primary for sure. It is a good thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:40.140
It is a good thing that Dianne Feinstein has&nbsp;
said. I've had a great run and she has. Longest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:45.840
serving senator, oldest senator. And it will&nbsp;
be very interesting to see the direction that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:51.240
California voters want to see their representation&nbsp;
go. So we will be certainly covering that race

